\doxysubsubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{xlio\_socket\_accept\_cb\_t}{xlio\_socket\_accept\_cb\_t}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily typedef void(\texorpdfstring{$\ast$}{*} xlio\+\_\+socket\+\_\+accept\+\_\+cb\+\_\+t) (\mbox{\hyperlink{group__xlio__socket_ga38bd8a56da936ea6bbced26cd3009588}{xlio\+\_\+socket\+\_\+t}} sock, \mbox{\hyperlink{group__xlio__socket_ga38bd8a56da936ea6bbced26cd3009588}{xlio\+\_\+socket\+\_\+t}} parent, uintptr\+\_\+t parent\+\_\+userdata\+\_\+sq)}



Accept callback function. 

This callback is invoked when a new connection is accepted on a listening socket. The new socket is automatically created and associated with the same polling group.


\begin{DoxyParams}{Parameters}
{\em sock} & The newly accepted socket \\
\hline
{\em parent} & The listening socket that accepted the connection \\
\hline
{\em parent\+\_\+userdata\+\_\+sq} & User data from the parent socket\\
\hline
\end{DoxyParams}
\begin{DoxyNote}{Note}
The new socket inherits the polling group from the parent but may need additional configuration (e.\+g., userdata\+\_\+sq update).
\end{DoxyNote}
